+# TPU v5e R interface amendment
+
+Proposed with U0011's scoped reference amendment; effective only on human installation.
+This is the exact semantic interface to implement, not executable schema admission.
+Normal generated-schema review and U0002 generation/adoption remain required before code
+installation. No ordinary reference job is executable merely because this text is installed.
+
+## Version and compatibility boundary
+
+Preserve ordinary /4, component model 2, TaskGraph/1 and observations/3 behavior unchanged.
+Add R roots `uarch-prepared/5` and `uarch-engine/5`, `uarch-taskgraph/2`, model
+`native-intervals` version `3` and engine `native-stage/3` in the same package/executable.
+The software package version follows its actual installed release; never manufacture a
+build identifier. R admission has checkpoint `R`, invocation `production|test`, and
+eligibility `reference_suite|verification_only`; test pairs only with verification_only.
+Version compatibility is explicit; /4 is not silently upgraded. No executable/source
+hashes, HostRecords, selectors or external reviewer artifacts are runtime inputs.
+
+Reuse the existing ordinary bundle/job/result data hashes, software/producer versions,
+rank, assumptions, source closure, mapped points, owner identities, per-op and completed
+work records. Validation and replay remain in the installed package. `source` for a decoder
+point carries its authenticated original v2 mathematical graph, selected decoder group and
+coefficient table. Head/tail work is not silently discarded from a whole-model request:
+the selected scope is explicitly one decoder layer. Preserve existing provenance data
+needed to interpret original v2 artifacts without adding new runtime attestation.
+
+## Narrow reference hardware branch
+
+Add `TpuV5eReference` as the R hardware branch rather than making every existing HardwareSpec
+field optional. Its literal identity is `tpu-v5e`, design_status=`reference`. All physical
+numbers carry SourcedValue provenance. A missing numeric leaf is represented as
+`{value:null, kind:claim, provenance:stub, source:null, unit:<declared unit>}`; it is not a
+permitted numeric input to a service law. Resolved required leaves must have compatible
+units and a positive value (latency may be zero only with explicit source/model support).
+Reference stipulations remain forbidden. Modeling policies and conservative allocation
+limits are in assumptions, never relabeled physical claims.
+
+The branch has this finite field inventory (no generic extra-fields map):
+
+| Group | Fields and types |
+| --- | --- |
+| Organization | `tensorcore_count`, `mxu_count`, `mxu_rows`, `mxu_cols`: sourced positive counts |
+| Published bounds | `bf16_peak_ops_per_s`, `int8_peak_ops_per_s`, `hbm_peak_bytes_per_s`: sourced positive rates |
+| Capacity | `hbm_capacity_bytes`, `vmem_capacity_bytes`, `smem_capacity_bytes`, `accumulator_bytes`, `operand_buffer_bytes`: sourced positive bytes or unknown |
+| Matrix service | `bf16_mxu_mac_per_s`, `int8_mxu_mac_per_s`: sourced positive rates or unknown; `matrix_startup_ps`, `matrix_issue_interval_ps`: sourced nonnegative ps or unknown |
+| Local transfer | `operand_bytes_per_s`, `vmem_bytes_per_s`: sourced positive byte/s or unknown |
+| HBM service | `hbm_latency_ps`, `hbm_issue_interval_ps`: sourced nonnegative ps or unknown; `hbm_max_outstanding`: sourced positive count or unknown |
+| Vector service | `arithmetic_ops_per_s`, `reduction_elements_per_s`, `exp_ops_per_s`, `reciprocal_ops_per_s`, `rsqrt_ops_per_s`, `cast_elements_per_s`: sourced positive rates or unknown; `vector_startup_ps`: sourced nonnegative ps or unknown |
+| Scalar/control | `scalar_ops_per_s`: sourced positive rate or unknown; `kernel_startup_ps`, `barrier_latency_ps`: sourced nonnegative ps or unknown |
+
+This inventory is a proposed abstraction, not proof these parameters can be sourced.
+No physical clock, physical channel count, 256-byte transaction, NoC route/port, DRAM
+refresh timing or energy field is read by this branch. Unknown nominal HBM capacity may
+be excluded from a timing read only if an explicit independently justified allocation
+limit bounds every buffer and is disclosed; otherwise allocation admission also refuses.
+Usable VMEM/SMEM budgets are explicit limits no larger than the resolved nominal capacity.
+Accumulator/staging capacity cannot be replaced by VMEM/SMEM nominal capacity.
+
+`assumptions` names this reference model, deterministic FIFO policy, shared-VMEM placement,
+logical-span HBM addressing and finite allocation budgets. Four equal matrix service shares,
+a single shared issue gate and aggregate HBM arbitration are **model choices**, not hardware
+facts. The selected numerical source/model must justify each required resolved timing input;
+public headline peaks do not populate these parameters automatically. Enumerate precisely
+which leaves were used, which were missing and which mechanisms were unrepresented.
+Production refuses any required unknown before executing events. No test-only bypass
+creates a reference prediction. Unused energy/physical topology must not be reported as zero.
+
+## Additive task and mathematical vocabulary
+
+Keep the existing OpSpec/PreparedOp and TaskGraph model; no second workload language.
+R mathematical ops accept the existing projection/decoder and v2 rotary operators, plus
+five narrowly specified OpSpec names for the selected microbenchmarks:
+
+- `stream_read_sum`: BF16 X[E] to FP32 Y[1]; E widening conversions and E-1 sum adds.
+- `stream_fill`: BF16 X[1] to BF16 Y[E]; runtime broadcast into distinct destination.
+- `stream_copy`: BF16 X[E] to BF16 Y[E]; disjoint materialized input/output ranges.
+- `paged_gather`: BF16 K/V pages, int32 page_index[P], BF16 contiguous K/V outputs;
+  B,Hkv,D,valid_tokens,block_tokens dimensions and exact page index values, bounded by
+  allocated page count. Valid payload and allocated bytes are separate.
+- `scalar_add`: two FP32 scalar inputs and one FP32 scalar output.
+
+Isolated matrix controls use the existing projection dot semantics with explicit M/K/N;
+INT8 controls are raw integer dots, not a quantized decoder. Add `int32` to R **storage and
+accumulator dtypes**, not to the generic rk-sim PrecisionFormat compute enum. Signed INT8
+inputs and INT32 output/accumulation have no scale operands in this scope. Maximum raw
+input magnitude and K bound are explicit; overflow-prone work refuses.
+
+R TaskGraph matrix compute adds `matrix_engine_index` (integer 0..3; core_id=0), supports
+K-reduction tile ranges and explicit partial-sum ownership. Matrix output conversion is
+performed once after all K slices, unless the mathematical graph explicitly contains an
+intermediate numeric boundary. Coverage validates a disjoint complete M/N/K partition,
+not just a sum equal to expected operations. `physical_extents` distinguishes issued
+padding from useful extents. Compiled masked work likewise stays distinct from useful
+causal pairs. No engine reconstructs or silently changes supplied mapping decisions.
+
+R vector/scalar tasks reference a mathematical op and explicit operand BufferRanges,
+operation class, element count and reduction axis/group extent. Their closed operation
+classes are add, multiply, compare, reduction_sum, reduction_max, exp, reciprocal, rsqrt,
+cast, broadcast and index. Cast records specify both storage dtypes. Counts and axis
+extents must be independently derivable from the bound mathematical op, not arbitrary
+caller-supplied delays or trusted expected totals. Fusion preserves each member's ID,
+work and numeric conversion points; it can remove only declared materializations.
+
+R buffers use existing ranges/lifetime rules with spaces hbm, vmem, smem and accumulator.
+MXU0..3 share the same VMEM namespace. R transfer records have logical source/destination
+ranges, payload_bytes, direction, op ownership and ordered spans. Physical transaction
+bytes/channel_id/route_id are absent in this aggregate model. Request boundaries are
+explicit **logical service** boundaries selected by the mapping, not assertions of physical
+transactions. Page tables, tails and copies cannot be synthesized during execution.
+
+Retain fixed bounds and overflow checks, with budgets sized to the finite selected suite;
+never silently truncate a graph. All malformed/unsupported data refuses before events.
+
+## Service, state and result obligations
+
+Within the same scheduler, staging/local transfers consume the declared byte service;
+matrices consume their assigned MXU and shared issue gate; vector/scalar operations consume
+their corresponding owner; HBM reads/writes share aggregate bandwidth and outstanding slots.
+A proposed tile service consists of explicit staging, startup/fill-drain and issued work
+intervals, with shared issue spacing, dependency/lifetime rules and only declared overlap.
+The exact numerical law/source is still the U0011 model decision; schema syntax or a
+ceiling-rate formula is not a verified timing law. Use checked rational ps arithmetic and
+ceil only at declared event boundaries. Do not route ps through an invented 1 Hz clock.
+Retain B's accepted next_edge behavior and issue-edge ordering in the clocked branch.
+
+Steady execution primes one complete iteration internally and reports the next; a second
+priming iteration is a comparison request. Persist declared physical residency and reset
+logical invocation state, per-iteration counters and scratch lifetimes. Full-layer logical
+KV length must not grow during warm-up of the same benchmark point. Only the reported
+iteration contributes counts, timing and critical-path attribution.
+
+New R observations carry actual executed matrix/vector/cast/scalar work and payload reads/
+writes, operation ownership, resource intervals, allocations and dependency/blocking causes.
+Physical transaction counts and unmodeled diagnostics are nullable, never manufactured.
+Keep existing analytic convention totals (for example 5*attention_pairs and 6*RMSNorm_elements)
+separate from typed executed primitive counts and conversion counts in R observations.
+Derive each from the same bound mathematics and verify the relation; never charge an exp,
+reduction and add identically just because the reporting convention calls each one op.
+Include scale/mask and numeric conversion work even when a historical analytic convention
+did not expose it. The /4 vector_ops equality must not be copied to an incompatible R
+count projection. Analytic and native comparisons must use the same declared count meaning.
+Preserve complete useful/issued counts, per-op work even for fused timing, total duration,
+critical-path sum and deterministic result hashes. Do not reuse observations/3 if its
+mandatory clock/transaction vocabulary cannot express these records; introduce R
+observations/4 and dispatch the single independent checker by admitted model/format.
+No result reports C1/accuracy solely from these types: verified timing semantics and the
+reviewed fidelity projection are prerequisites; unmodeled/error/energy retain honest scope.
